From 533ddb7663784fa51a5a0f580b140867558566ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andreas Helbech Kleist <andreaskleist@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 08:34:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] media: ipu6: Don't close unopened ISYS firmware on
 runtime suspend

The ISYS firmware is opened in isys_runtime_pm_resume() and closed in
isys_runtime_pm_suspend(), but the device can be runtime suspended
without the resume callback having run: after the PCI device is reset
and the driver rebound, the ISYS probe is deferred and the device later
suspends with no firmware context, and ipu6_fw_com_close() dereferences
NULL.

Only close the firmware if it was opened.

Fixes: 70e3fac3ec78 ("media: ipu6: Move firmware init/cleanup to RPM callbacks")
Signed-off-by: Andreas Helbech Kleist <andreaskleist@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu6-isys.c | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu6-isys.c b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu6-isys.c
index c00ae9eb6..ef1100c2c 100644
--- a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu6-isys.c
+++ b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu6-isys.c
@@ -883,10 +883,14 @@ static int isys_runtime_pm_suspend(struct device *dev)
 	struct ipu6_device *isp = adev->isp;
 	int ret = 0;
 
-	isys->adev->auxdrv_data->fw_ops->close(isys);
+	/* Runtime active does not imply the firmware was opened. */
 	if (isys->fwctx) {
-		dev_warn(&isys->adev->auxdev.dev, "failed to close fw isys\n");
-		ret = -EIO;
+		isys->adev->auxdrv_data->fw_ops->close(isys);
+		if (isys->fwctx) {
+			dev_warn(&isys->adev->auxdev.dev,
+				 "failed to close fw isys\n");
+			ret = -EIO;
+		}
 	}
 
 	mutex_lock(&isys->mutex);
-- 
